  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Nevada's 1st Congressional District pits seven-term Democratic incumbent Dina Titus against Republican state Senator Carrie Buck, along with several nonpartisan candidates. The district covers central Las Vegas, Paradise, Henderson, and Boulder City in Clark County. Titus has held the seat since 2013 and won re-election with 52.0% in 2024; Buck flipped a state Senate seat from Democratic to Republican in 2020 and has emerged as a well-funded challenger. The race is rated as 'Likely Democratic' by Cook Political Report and 'Lean Democratic' by Inside Elections, though Republican gains in the district could make it competitive.",
  "polling": [],
  "polling_note": "No independent general election head-to-head polls specific to the NV-01 race between Titus and Buck were found as of mid-2026. A Navigator Research battleground survey (Feb 2026) included NV-01 among 62 battleground districts but did not release district-level horse-race numbers. Cook Political Report rates the race 'Likely D' and Sabato's Crystal Ball rates it 'Likely D' as of mid-2025.",
