      "name": "Dina Titus",
      "party": "Democratic Party",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Dina Titus is the incumbent U.S. Representative for Nevada's 1st Congressional District, first elected in 2012 after previously serving one term in the 3rd district (2009\u20132011). She spent 20 years in the Nevada Senate and was the Democratic nominee for governor in 2006. A former political science professor at UNLV, Titus focuses on healthcare, education, and consumer protection, and is expected to become the dean of Nevada's congressional delegation in 2027.",
